ManaUser <look@sig.invalid> writes:

> letters, q for the sack, x or the pick, and so on. But I've noticed
> recently that when I stash the pick in the sack in order to enter a store,
> the next item I pick up is x. This despite the fact that my inventory is
> nowhere near full.

When the game assigns inventory letters to items you pick up, it only
checks that it doesn't assign a letter already used by something already
IN your inventory. It doesn't check which inventory letters have been
assigned to items in containers you may be carrying, or to items you have
dropped or that have otherwise left your inventory list.

In other words, when an item leaves your inventory, it loses its
reservation for an inventory letter. 
When you pick it up or take out of a container again, the game checks
which letter it has used before, and assigns it back IF nothing else is
using the letter then. 

I haven't studied the source for how letters are assigned for things you
pick up, but I suspect the game remembers which letter was assigned most
recently and picks the next available letter. So, if the object most
recently picked up got letter x, the next object gets letter y no matter
if letter l is available or not.

However, Pasi Kallinen wrote a fixinv patch for Nethack 3.4.2 to change
this behavior. I haven't tried it and don't know whether or not it works
with 3.4.3, but it can be found at 
http://cs.joensuu.fi/~pkalli/code/nh342-fixinv.diff

